   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Green Eyed Lady tease**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Feedback Jam**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2008-07-19.core** (recommended): source not stated; 32 songs; 168 min [1]\n- **ween2008-07-19.akg414.flac16**: source not stated; 32 songs; 161 min [2]\n- **ween2008-07-19**: source not stated; 32 songs; 168 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Gene plays drums first, then Dean takes over drums while Claude moves to bass; Dean wrecks the drum kit [1]\n- Gene drums first, then Dean takes the kit and Claude plays bass; Dean ends up destroying the drums [2]\n- Gene starts on drums, then Dean takes over with Claude on bass, and Dean smashes up the kit [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2008-07-19.core**: taped by Chris King; transferred by Chris King; source: Cores In Line Core Pre Amp > M-audio1 (24/96) [1]. Also: Core microphones into a Core preamp, then M-audio recorder at 24/96, CF card, dithered to 16/44 and encoded to FLAC [1]\n- **ween2008-07-19.akg414.flac16**: taped by Dean Lambrecht; transferred by Dean Lambrecht; source: AKG C 414b xls (AB hypers 5'ROC FOB, stand 12.5'^) > Hi Ho Silver xlr's > UA5 (BM2p+ mod.) > JB3 (opti) @ 44.1 kHz. [2]\n- **ween2008-07-19**: taped by Chris King; transferred by Chris King; source: Church-Audio STC-11> Church-Audio ST-9100 > M-audio2 (24/96) [3]. Also: Church-Audio STC-11 mics into an ST-9100 preamp, then M-audio recorder at 24/96, CF card, dithered to 16/44 and FLAC [3]",
